=== sg_compare_and_write ===
DESCRIPTION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Performs a SCSI COMPARE AND WRITE operation. Sends a double size buffer, the
first half is used to compare what is at LBA for NUM blocks. If and only if
the comparison is equal, then the second half of the buffer is written to
LBA for NUM blocks.


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  sg_compare_and_write [--dpo] [--fua] [--fua_nv] [--grpnum=GN] [--help]
      --in=IF|--inc=IF [--inw=WF] --lba=LBA [--num=NUM] [--quiet]
      [--timeout=TO] [--verbose] [--version] [--wrprotect=WP]
      [--xferlen=LEN] DEVICE


POSITIONALS (1) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  DEVICE


FLAGS (16) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Where
-d, --dpo          set the dpo bit in cdb (def: clear)
-f, --fua          set the fua bit in cdb (def: clear)
-F, --fua_nv       set the fua_nv bit in cdb (def: clear)
-g, --grpnum GN    GN is GROUP NUMBER to set in cdb (def: 0)
-h, --help         print out usage message
-i, --in IF        IF is a file containing a compare buffer and optionally a
                   write buffer (when --inw=WF is not given)
-C, --inc IF       The same as the --in option
-D, --inw WF       WF is a file containing a write buffer
-l, --lba LBA      LBA of the first block to compare and write
-n, --num NUM      number of blocks to compare/write (def: 1)
-q, --quiet        suppress MISCOMPARE report to stderr, still sets exit
                   status of 14
-t, --timeout TO   timeout for the command (def: 60 secs)
-v, --verbose      increase verbosity (use '-vv' for more)
-V, --version      print version string then exit
-w, --wrprotect WP write protect information (def: 0)
-x, --xferlen LEN  number of bytes to transfer. Default is (2
                   * NUM
                   * 512) or 1024 when NUM is 1
